1
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,580
I kicked a pebble and sent
it flying until it was gone

3
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:29,420
While talking to the head of the gym class

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
They laughed at me for
staying so full of energy

5
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I stir up some good spirit somewhere

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
There's only winning, no other way

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A single nightmare, the unchanging streets

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
Are gentler than ever

9
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,700
The sun has already gone down

11
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,940
Yakitori, stuffed in my mouth

12
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,840
Even just to look at it...

13
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:57,500
Of the pointed hat

14
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:04,080
The sun sinks from the
waterworks toward Ōishi Electric

15
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:10,100
Tomorrow too,
it'll end with something dropped, won't it

16
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:13,660
Katsushika,
for a while I lost even my happiness

17
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I've only just realized, it's me

18
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:30,120
Gah!

19
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:32,400
Dizzy... everything's spinning!

20
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:33,500
Mmmm...

21
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:36,460
Mm...

22
00:01:36,460 --> 00:01:37,460
Mm...

23
00:01:37,460 --> 00:01:40,360
Mm...

24
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:43,880
Mm...

25
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:48,640
Oh my...

26
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:50,620
I worked!

27
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:51,220
Eee...

28
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:53,100
Don't raise your voice, it echoes.

29
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:55,620
A terrible hangover,
for the first time in ages.

30
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:00,360
Why are we sleeping in a place like this?

31
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:01,420
I think

32
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:03,260
Let's hit one more place!

33
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:04,540
Eiji

34
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:08,980
You remember up to the fifth izakaya, right?

35
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:12,120
Me? I don't remember anything
after the third place.

36
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:17,220
Where's the senior officer?

37
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:19,340
Senpai!

38
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,520
Excuse me.

39
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:25,160
Amazing, Ryotsu.

40
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,860
Did he already go to work?

41
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:30,380
Flower child, Ryo-chan.

42
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:43,400
What's this? Is my face funny or something?

43
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:45,400
Yeah, it's funny.

44
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,260
I see. I see.

45
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:49,880
I wonder what's wrong with everyone.

46
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:52,540
A police officer!

47
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:54,580
Yes, yes, that's right.

48
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:57,360
Thank you for your hard work on the job.

49
00:02:58,180 --> 00:02:58,660
Mm-hmm.

50
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:03,140
Everyone,
let's wave goodbye to the police officer.

51
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:04,140
Bye-bye!

52
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:04,660
Bye!

53
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:10,760
Looks like it's going
to be a good day today.

54
00:03:22,860 --> 00:03:26,200
From kindergarteners to
grandpas and grandmas,

55
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:28,940
Ryo-san's really on a roll with popularity

56
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:33,860
What's Ryo-san thinking this time?

57
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:35,580
He's so carefree, isn't he.

58
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:39,080
What's he up to?

59
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:40,980
Is this some kind of punishment game?

60
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:43,640
It's funny how it doesn't suit him at all.

61
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:47,160
Hey, what are you muttering
about this whole time?

62
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:51,180
I was just wondering what
the senior officer is doing.

63
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:51,580
Right, right.

64
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:57,180
What do you mean? I promised to submit
last month's incident report by lunch today.

65
00:03:57,180 --> 00:03:59,680
Forget the Chief.
Anyway, just pass me some tea.

66
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:01,040
Some hot tea.

67
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:04,060
Wouldn't it be better to
give him water instead of tea?

68
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:05,480
Right?

69
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:10,220
Oh my.

70
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:12,820
What a pretty flower.

71
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,380
It caught my eye.

72
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,780
What are you doing, Reiko?

73
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:19,940
Oh no, it's you, Ryo-chan?

74
00:04:19,940 --> 00:04:21,700
Do I look like a potted plant to you?

75
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:24,860
But on Ryo-chan's head...

76
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:25,940
Head.

77
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:31,660
Flowers?

78
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:36,880
There are flowers blooming on your head.

79
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:41,160
You didn't notice?

80
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:45,460
Now, at Showa Kinen Park,
the cosmos are in full bloom.

81
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:46,800
Just one look at these flowers

82
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:49,740
explains why everyone
passing by was laughing at me.

83
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:53,080
These flowers have really
taken root in my head.

84
00:04:53,080 --> 00:04:55,020
Wow, how unusual.

85
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:57,540
Or rather, I've never seen anything like it.

86
00:04:58,780 --> 00:05:00,560
Someone who grows real flowers like that...

87
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:02,960
My head is itchy.

88
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,620
What are you doing, Ryo-chan?

89
00:05:05,620 --> 00:05:06,900
Why are you pulling them out?

90
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:09,400
Putting these old-fashioned,
scorched-looking flowers on me...

91
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:10,700
Hang on a minute.

92
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:11,180
How embarrassing.

93
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:15,120
Come on, there's no need to pull them out.

94
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:17,560
Yeah, they're blooming so beautifully.

95
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:18,800
It'd be a waste.

96
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:20,860
They actually suit you, Ryo-san.

97
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:21,720
Don't mess with me.

98
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:25,120
Once a man grows flowers on his head,
he's finished.

99
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:27,440
Do you think so?

100
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:32,420
What's wrong with having flowers?
They're cute.

101
00:05:32,940 --> 00:05:36,220
Cute my foot! Would you ask
directions from a cop like this?

102
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:39,540
A citizen asking a flower-headed
cop for help? No way!

103
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:42,120
I'll give the directions.

104
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:43,280
Me too.

105
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:43,820
Me too.

106
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:47,280
That's not what I meant.

107
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:52,560
Anyway, Ryo-san, you always find
giving directions too much of a hassle.

108
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:56,060
Excuse me, where's the post office?

109
00:05:56,460 --> 00:05:58,900
Ask the mailbox about the post office.

110
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,020
Yo-san.

111
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:07,100
So directions don't matter right now,
do they?

112
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:09,140
They do matter, you know.

113
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:09,820
Yeah, they do.

114
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:11,500
Since we're on the subject,
let me say something.

115
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:14,260
The main duties of police
officers at a police box are

116
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:17,060
giving directions, traffic control,
and enforcing the law.

117
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:19,500
I know that without you telling me.

118
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,260
Today's theme is

119
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:25,240
flowers on my head, these days.
What's wrong with that?

120
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:27,680
What kind of flower is this?

121
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:28,980
Reiko, do you know?

122
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:33,460
It's not a tulip or a gerbera.
I've never seen this flower before.

123
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:36,440
I don't care what kind of flower it is.

124
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:38,640
But it smells really nice.

125
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:39,280
It really does.

126
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:41,800
Let's take one photo for memories.

127
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:45,000
Hey, don't just pick them off!

128
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,020
Me too.

129
00:06:46,020 --> 00:06:46,820
Can I join in too?

130
00:06:46,820 --> 00:06:48,280
Say cheese!

131
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:52,300
Hey, hey, if you're going to take them,
you'd better pay me 100 yen each!

132
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:52,700
Fine.

133
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:56,600
But why did flowers bloom
on the senior officer's head?

134
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:58,520
Don't you have any idea why?

135
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,120
How would I know that?

136
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:04,500
Come to think of it,
I haven't taken a bath in about two weeks.

137
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:06,900
Ryo-chan, gross!

138
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:10,280
Maybe it's because you're so filthy that it was
easy for them to draw nutrients from your scalp.

139
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:11,740
While he's distracted -

140
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:15,940
Ow!

141
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:19,120
These things really have
rooted themselves into my head!

142
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:22,720
Damn it, I almost became an express train!

143
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:29,720
Look, these flowers have already wilted.

144
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:32,740
They withered because they can't
get nutrients from Ryo-san anymore.

145
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:34,280
Poor things.

146
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:38,720
D-don't look at me with those accusing eyes.

147
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:40,600
For now, take a photo of these flowers.

148
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:44,700
Try sending them to Nakagawa Trading's
flora and fauna research facility.

149
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:46,040
I'll have them investigated.

150
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:52,637
Damn it, because of that Anahana,
we're late for our appointment!

151
00:07:52,687 --> 00:07:53,520
Well, I did it already.

152
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:55,320
Do you think I upset her?

153
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:57,860
Hehe, all the way over there.

154
00:07:58,180 --> 00:08:01,420
Why is everyone staring at me?

155
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:02,720
What's that?!

156
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,540
Ugh, how stupid.

157
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:06,660
What is it?

158
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:08,240
No way!

159
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:13,880
Aaaah! It's in there again!

160
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,420
What are you sticking on there, you caveman.

161
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:18,700
Though it's kind of cute.

162
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:22,198
I just pulled them out,
and they're already growing back.

163
00:08:22,248 --> 00:08:24,340
What on earth has happened to me?

164
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:27,100
The incident report was due today,
wasn't it, Ryotsu?

165
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:27,560
Yes.

166
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:29,560
Chief!

167
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:32,320
What do you think you're doing?

168
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:35,540
W-well I wrote the incident report, Chief.

169
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:40,560
I'm asking what those leaves on your head
that look like bamboo dragonflies are.

170
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:42,100
So this is...

171
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:44,560
Is this your petty revenge for
making you write that incident report?

172
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,020
No, Chief.

173
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:49,280
Then is your goal to tarnish the
authority of the Katsushika station?

174
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:51,400
No, they just sprouted on their own.

175
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:53,740
Even when I pull them out,
they pop right back up like bamboo shoots.

176
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:56,240
That's ridiculous, you idiot!

177
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:59,920
How far do you intend to push
me before you're satisfied?

178
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:02,300
No, no, that's why, Chief, the skin...

179
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:05,540
Stop it! My scalp is stretching!

180
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:06,660
The flower...

181
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:08,200
W-what?

182
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:12,860
Look, there are flowers blooming

183
00:09:14,180 --> 00:09:17,960
I told you, they're really
growing from my head, the flowers!

184
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,980
Flowers from my head!

185
00:09:19,980 --> 00:09:23,360
And they won't come out,
the flowers from my head!

186
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:24,720
Wow, that's amazing.

187
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:25,980
That's incredible.

188
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:28,240
They really are growing. How creepy.

189
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:32,480
Idiot!

190
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,200
Why?

191
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:37,600
Flowers bloom because you're slacking off!
Pull yourself together!

192
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:39,540
That's so unreasonable!

193
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:42,380
Listen,
get rid of those flowers by tomorrow.

194
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:45,580
Let's go.

195
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:53,580
The garden shears aren't cutting it.

196
00:09:53,580 --> 00:09:57,640
They came out easily this morning,
but they're getting stronger and stronger.

197
00:09:57,640 --> 00:09:59,800
Shut up!

198
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:03,320
This is all your fault
for leaving me behind,

199
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:06,060
which is why these, these flowers sprouted!

200
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:08,440
Take responsibility and
get rid of them properly!

201
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,740
My heart aches a little.

202
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:17,960
Just do it already.

203
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:18,460
Alright.

204
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:23,400
W-what's wrong?

205
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:28,080
Next, next!

206
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:33,480
Alam

207
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:03,700
Together!

208
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:06,520
Here we go!

209
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:07,540
Mr. Ryotsu!

210
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:10,580
Yeah, Honda, just do it in one go!

211
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:12,360
Hold on to me tight!

212
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,100
Okay!

213
00:11:13,780 --> 00:11:15,520
Rider form!

214
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:17,320
Heave-ho!

215
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,240
Heave-ho!

216
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,060
Heave-ho!

217
00:11:19,060 --> 00:11:20,000
Heave!

218
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:20,360
Heave!

219
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:20,720
Heave!

220
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:21,100
Heave!

221
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:31,840
Orio

222
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:32,480
Derrick...

223
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:33,860
Derrick sense!

224
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,620
Go, go, go, go, go!

225
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:41,240
Heave!

226
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,760
Come on, come on, come on!

227
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,340
Ow ow

228
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:48,380
Move, move, move, move, move, move!

229
00:11:51,180 --> 00:11:52,360
Bachi Shiguru!

230
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:54,880
Gaga-gaga-gaga!

231
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:57,540
Has it come out yet, Ryotsu-no-danna?

232
00:11:58,380 --> 00:12:00,400
It just hurts, and it won't budge at all!

233
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:04,280
Do something!

234
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:19,821
This morning,

235
00:12:19,871 --> 00:12:23,620
we got a call from the president of
Nagakawa Bussan about these flowers.

236
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,720
These are truly ancient flowers
that should have gone extinct.

237
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:32,340
Andre the Giant Amigo Yamato

238
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:33,640
Take a look.

239
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:36,260
Once again, it's that Ryotsu Kankichi.

240
00:12:56,560 --> 00:13:00,020
Looks like I'm stuck living
with this thing for a while.

241
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:04,360
Whoa, a bee! Careful, careful!

242
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,140
Whoa, what the hell?

243
00:13:14,140 --> 00:13:14,703
Damn,

244
00:13:14,753 --> 00:13:18,640
Lured in by the sweet scent of these flowers

245
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:19,920
Damn.

246
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:30,260
Whaaaaat?

247
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:44,000
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

248
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,260
Yah, got it! Pulled it free!

249
00:13:45,260 --> 00:13:48,580
W-what the--!

250
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:51,880
What the hell are you doing, hey!

251
00:13:52,680 --> 00:13:54,900
Don't you dare hurt my nose!

252
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:58,120
Hey! I've seen you before!
I've definitely seen you before!

253
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:16,780
My name is Doctor Seriza.

254
00:14:16,780 --> 00:14:22,100
I have thoroughly examined your
body and the nose on your head.

255
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:26,640
And an astonishing fact has come to light.

256
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,140
I remember!

257
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:31,060
The quack doctor who
examined my body back then!

258
00:14:31,540 --> 00:14:32,120
Quack?

259
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:36,800
That's enough.

260
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:40,240
We'd be in trouble if the
precious nose were harmed.

261
00:14:41,160 --> 00:14:43,360
Nose? You're after this nose?

262
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,220
Fine, I don't need it,
so just pull it out quickly!

263
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:48,800
That's not possible.

264
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:49,900
Why?!

265
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:52,540
This is your skull and brain.

266
00:14:52,540 --> 00:14:55,640
As you can see, the roots of the
nose are wrapped tightly around them.

267
00:14:57,220 --> 00:14:59,940
If you pull out the nose,
the brain will definitely come out too.

268
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:01,660
N-no, not the brain!

269
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,900
Yes, that's right. So I won't pull it out.

270
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:07,960
Why does this have to happen to me...

271
00:15:08,460 --> 00:15:10,580
That's exactly the problem.

272
00:15:14,060 --> 00:15:17,810
This is a Homo erectus from
about 550,000 years ago,

273
00:15:17,860 --> 00:15:20,260
and a fossilized flower
that lived during that time.

274
00:15:20,260 --> 00:15:21,062
Liar,

275
00:15:21,112 --> 00:15:25,160
how could a fossil this old
and this perfect still be around?

276
00:15:29,820 --> 00:15:35,860
This is an exact model, restored from
a fossil fragment and detailed data.

277
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:39,540
Me?

278
00:15:40,140 --> 00:15:40,540
Yes.

279
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:45,540
You, with a constitution very close to that
of an early human from 550,000 years ago,

280
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:48,980
and an ancient flower seed
that miraculously survived,

281
00:15:48,980 --> 00:15:51,585
came together somehow, met,

282
00:15:51,635 --> 00:15:54,700
fused, sprouted, grew, and bloomed.

283
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:58,400
This truly can be called
nothing but a miracle.

284
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:00,960
For me, it's just a calamity.

285
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:04,780
You have a duty to preserve those flowers.

286
00:16:04,780 --> 00:16:06,360
Mr. Kankichi Ryotsu,

287
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:10,080
early to bed, early to rise,
and an afternoon walk.

288
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:13,540
Meals should be lightly seasoned natural food,
and no alcohol, all right?

289
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:14,440
What is this?

290
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:18,540
From now on, for the sake of
the flowers' health and safety,

291
00:16:18,540 --> 00:16:22,060
you will have to practice
thorough self-restraint.

292
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:22,840
Don't be ridiculous!

293
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:26,320
Why should I go that far for a
bunch of flowers I've never even met?

294
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:28,740
You have no choice in the matter.

295
00:16:28,740 --> 00:16:32,680
This matter has already
become a national project.

296
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:33,900
Ryotsu-kun.

297
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:45,220
So this is the 550,000-year-old flower,
Ohara-kun?

298
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:47,380
Yes, so it seems.

299
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:50,000
Good thing we didn't pull it out.

300
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:54,340
Then, starting today, you will be solely
responsible for guarding this flower.

301
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:57,651
Hey, Chief. This guy is tougher than I am,

302
00:16:57,701 --> 00:16:59,500
so he'll be fine even if we leave him alone.

303
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:00,800
Ryotsu.

304
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:04,840
This is also a direct order
from the Commissioner-General.

305
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:06,480
The Commissioner-General...

306
00:17:06,840 --> 00:17:09,260
Please, I'm counting on you, Ohara-kun.

307
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:09,920
Yes, sir!

308
00:17:11,940 --> 00:17:12,780
Excuse me.

309
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:22,080
That's not fair! You're dumping all the hassle on
me while you and the Chief just sit back and relax!

310
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:23,200
What did you say?

311
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:26,840
If it's going to be like this, I should've
gotten rid of it before anyone found out.

312
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:33,400
Don't be ridiculous! Think of it as looking after a valuable guest.
Guard that flower, understand?

313
00:17:35,380 --> 00:17:39,720
That's right, for this valuable guest,
give me a week of refresh leave!

314
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:43,640
If we took it to a southern island
and let it soak up plenty of sunshine,

315
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:45,940
I'm sure the guest would be happy too.

316
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:47,080
No way.

317
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:47,860
Why not?

318
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:49,680
Once I take my eyes off you,

319
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:51,980
you'll only end up causing trouble.

320
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:54,320
You'd just spend all day in your
room playing with models and games,

321
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:57,160
and before long you'd be living a
lazy life with night and day reversed.

322
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:59,380
It's as plain as day.

323
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:01,880
To live a regular, disciplined life,

324
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:04,720
staying on as a police officer
is the best thing for you.

325
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:07,920
Forget vacation.
Starting today, you get no days off at all.

326
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:08,580
Hey, come on...

327
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:12,100
This is awful.

328
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:15,320
Are you okay, Ryo-chan? You look so gaunt.

329
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:17,500
I'm starving.

330
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:22,760
Senpai,
they've taken away all of your pleasures.

331
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:26,600
I don't need pleasures. Just let me eat.

332
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:30,580
Ancient rice, miso soup, and a few pickles.

333
00:18:31,020 --> 00:18:32,280
Plain food every day.

334
00:18:32,280 --> 00:18:35,280
I know it's hard for you, Ryo-san,
feeling like you're already retired,

335
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,760
but plain food is good for the body.

336
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:40,500
I'm starving.

337
00:18:40,550 --> 00:18:44,371
Day after day, with just one of these lunch boxes,
I'm going to die soon!

338
00:18:44,421 --> 00:18:47,780
The flowers will wither too.
Is that what you want, Reiko?

339
00:18:48,240 --> 00:18:50,083
It's a shame for Ryo-chan,

340
00:18:50,133 --> 00:18:52,280
but the flower is blooming so beautifully.

341
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:56,060
I'm fulfilling my duty admirably, senpai.

342
00:18:57,120 --> 00:18:59,734
It's your fault. You're the one to blame.

343
00:18:59,784 --> 00:19:03,160
Thanks to you, I'm a living fossil anyway.

344
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:07,160
I'm starving.
I want something rich and greasy.

345
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:11,020
Stuffing my stomach full of greasy food.

346
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:12,380
Kameari Park box, Unit 8, dispatching.

347
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:16,840
What? A hostage standoff at the Chinese
restaurant in front of the station?

348
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:21,220
What? Chinese food? What? Chinese food?

349
00:19:21,260 --> 00:19:21,660
Yoisho!

350
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:30,080
Three million yen in cash and a car.
Hurry up!

351
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:31,060
Hurry up!

352
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:36,120
It's dangerous, so please step back.

353
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:38,560
If you don't want to get hurt, back off.

354
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:43,140
What's the situation?
Do we know who the suspect is?

355
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:45,460
The suspect appears to be a
former employee of this restaurant.

356
00:19:45,460 --> 00:19:48,380
The other employees and all the customers
inside have already been evacuated, sir.

357
00:19:48,820 --> 00:19:52,140
Right, deploy the emergency units now,
without letting the suspect notice us.

358
00:19:52,140 --> 00:19:52,400
Yes, sir!

359
00:19:57,460 --> 00:20:00,600
Isn't that Ryotsu over there, Ohara?

360
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:02,340
Chinese food!

361
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:07,980
Didn't I tell you!
Where's the bulletproof case?

362
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:10,520
What do you think you're doing?
If anything happens to the precious flower!

363
00:20:10,620 --> 00:20:14,200
Chinese food over flowers,
not the hostages, not the shumai,

364
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:15,760
lives are on the line!

365
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:17,160
Ugh!

366
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:20,380
Danger is calling out to the town!

367
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:21,800
Ryo-san! Ryo-san!

368
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:26,200
It's him!
Hurry up, or the hostages won't live!

369
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:27,220
Hurry up!

370
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:28,620
Help!

371
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:41,500
This fragrant smell is hoppōsai.

372
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:42,580
Ginger pork loin.

373
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:43,860
Hoikōrō.

374
00:20:57,780 --> 00:20:59,260
What's with all the noise? Shut up.

375
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:00,200
The flower moved.

376
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:01,400
That flower over there, just now.

377
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:02,340
Flower?

378
00:21:05,060 --> 00:21:07,040
The flower's moving, you idiot.

379
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:08,040
Flower.

380
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:09,380
That's strange.

381
00:21:09,380 --> 00:21:11,420
Are you half-asleep, you idiot?

382
00:21:11,420 --> 00:21:14,220
The flower's shrinking,
it's about to run out of energy.

383
00:21:18,320 --> 00:21:19,820
Senior Ryo-san.

384
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:23,780
Let's go.

385
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:30,540
See, I told you it's moving, bro.

386
00:21:30,540 --> 00:21:31,380
What?

387
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:35,940
Are you okay?

388
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:39,780
Something's burning.

389
00:21:46,140 --> 00:21:48,260
My Chinese food...

390
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:53,140
Look, bro, that flower's moving after all!

391
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:58,680
Bro!

392
00:22:03,540 --> 00:22:06,580
What do you plan to do if
anything happens to that flower?

393
00:22:06,580 --> 00:22:08,760
Then I'll take responsibility...

394
00:22:08,760 --> 00:22:12,060
This won't be settled by
your head alone, Ohara.

395
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:20,640
But there's a flower on the cop's head!

396
00:22:20,640 --> 00:22:22,760
Gemerujogujogii!

397
00:22:23,440 --> 00:22:25,060
Look, gyoza!

398
00:22:25,060 --> 00:22:25,740
Charge in!

399
00:22:35,140 --> 00:22:35,720
Ryotsu!

400
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:38,340
Ryotsu! Where did he go?

401
00:22:47,320 --> 00:22:51,000
My pork buns, my shumai!

402
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,420
Mac's attack!

403
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:18,920
Come on!

404
00:23:29,320 --> 00:23:30,680
Ryo-san

405
00:23:32,080 --> 00:23:35,380
The get-well flowers from Director Seriza...

406
00:23:37,380 --> 00:23:40,080
I hate noses! I hate noses!

407
00:24:07,460 --> 00:24:08,420
Everyday

408
00:24:08,420 --> 00:24:13,980
Blueprints and all,
crumpled into a reprimand and tossed away.

409
00:24:15,040 --> 00:24:17,480
Bare instincts, naked instincts.

410
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:18,520
Playing the fool,

411
00:24:19,420 --> 00:24:22,300
reckless and broke,
and that's fine, isn't it?

412
00:24:23,860 --> 00:24:28,080
I'll just do it my way,
doing whatever I want.

413
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:32,640
Chief Ohara's thunder, smoke from the head.

414
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:36,100
Run away and you'll get
hauled up like a turtle.

415
00:24:37,380 --> 00:24:38,260
Ohoo!

416
00:24:38,260 --> 00:24:39,880
In the flowering Edo,

417
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:40,360
Just a moment,

418
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:42,080
Ryōzan taigun,

419
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:42,880
thanks as always,

420
00:24:42,880 --> 00:24:45,440
Fūraimatsu,

421
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:46,640
Atarakamo play,

422
00:24:46,640 --> 00:24:47,560
9×2,

423
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:49,060
Jugemu jugemu,

424
00:24:49,060 --> 00:24:50,240
gokō no surikire,

425
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:51,320
kaijari suigyo,

426
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:52,800
suigyo-matsu.

427
00:24:52,800 --> 00:24:53,680
Gungyo-matsu

428
00:24:53,680 --> 00:24:54,540
Furai-matsu

429
00:24:54,540 --> 00:24:55,780
Kuu neru tokoro ni

430
00:24:55,780 --> 00:24:56,420
Sumu tokoro

431
00:24:56,920 --> 00:24:58,100
Yabura kōji

432
00:24:58,100 --> 00:24:58,820
Bura kōji

433
00:24:58,820 --> 00:25:00,080
Paipo paipo paipo

434
00:25:00,080 --> 00:25:01,280
Shūringan

435
00:25:01,280 --> 00:25:02,240
Shūringan no

436
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:03,100
Gūrindai

437
00:25:03,100 --> 00:25:04,400
Gūrindai no

438
00:25:04,400 --> 00:25:05,380
Ponpoko pī no

439
00:25:05,380 --> 00:25:06,320
Ponpoko nā no

440
00:25:14,420 --> 00:25:15,520
Hi, everyone, hello!

441
00:25:16,020 --> 00:25:17,700
I'm the idol of Katsushika Police Station.

442
00:25:17,700 --> 00:25:18,820
I'm Kumawari-kun!

443
00:25:19,180 --> 00:25:20,600
If you copy me,

444
00:25:20,600 --> 00:25:22,820
everyone will become such good kids.

445
00:25:23,380 --> 00:25:25,240
First, when you're about to get scolded,

446
00:25:25,240 --> 00:25:26,180
One, two, three!

447
00:25:26,560 --> 00:25:27,920
Sorry, Chief.

448
00:25:28,800 --> 00:25:31,340
Next time, fight, Kumawari-kun!

449
00:25:31,820 --> 00:25:32,500
Nice to meet you.

450
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:35,740
Over there is Kame-ari.

451
00:25:36,780 --> 00:25:38,940
Well, I'm sure there's Kame-ari.

452
00:25:39,880 --> 00:25:44,240
Everyone, come to our town!

453
00:25:45,060 --> 00:25:45,820
Thank you.

